@startuml
title Portfolio Demo - Logical Architecture (8aa4035b audit + #327 removal/deploy/probe closure, 2026-09-26)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Demo user" as User
node "Azure demo application boundary" {
  component "Static Web Apps\nNext.js static export" as Frontend
  component "External ingress\napi-gateway / WebFlux" as Gateway
  component "Internal ingress\nportfolio-service / MVC" as Portfolio
  component "Internal ingress\nmarket-data-service / MVC" as Market
  component "Internal ingress\ninsight-service / MVC" as Insight
  component "Separate market refresh Job\n08:00 UTC schedule" as Refresh
  component "Separate market repair Job\nmanual trigger only / fenced MM.NS repair" as Repair
}

database "External PostgreSQL\nidentity, holdings/version, price projection/history" as Postgres
database "External MongoDB\nstored market prices/references" as Mongo
queue "External Kafka\nmarket-prices / PriceUpdatedEvent" as Kafka
database "External Redis\nlimits/presence, observations, AI caches" as Redis
cloud "Yahoo market-data provider" as Yahoo
cloud "Azure OpenAI\nconfigured adapters / managed identity" as AI
cloud "FX provider\nUSD rate feed" as FX
component "OTLP agent / Application Insights\nsource-configured telemetry" as Telemetry

User --> Frontend : UI
Frontend --> Gateway : HTTPS JSON / separate API origin
Gateway --> Postgres : signup / login credentials
Gateway --> Redis : limiter / advisory presence
Gateway --> Portfolio : /api/portfolio/**, /api/assets/**
Gateway --> Market : /api/market/**
Gateway --> Insight : /api/insights/**, /api/chat/**
Portfolio --> Postgres : transactional holdings / analytics
Portfolio --> FX : available FX conversion
Market --> Mongo : stored reads / key-gated internal seed
Market --> Kafka : internal-seed observations (public POST removed)
Refresh --> Yahoo : scheduled price fetch
Refresh --> Mongo : persist observations
Refresh --> Kafka : keyed price publication
Repair --> Mongo : fenced legacy MM.NS to M&M.NS repair
Kafka --> Portfolio : portfolio-group projection
Kafka --> Insight : insight-group cache updates
Portfolio --> Kafka : rejected/exhausted records to market-prices.DLT
Insight --> Redis : prices / observation window / caches
Insight --> AI : optional resolution / sentiment
Gateway ..> Telemetry : observations
Portfolio ..> Telemetry : observations
Market ..> Telemetry : observations
Insight ..> Telemetry : observations
Refresh ..> Telemetry : observations

note bottom of Kafka
  Persist/publish is not a cross-store transaction or outbox.
  Consumer projection/cache semantics differ; no exactly-once claim.
end note
note bottom of Insight
  Bulk summaries use stored facts without model calls.
  Source labels can describe cached sentiment.
  Historical path-ID advisor IDOR is CLOSED by route removal (#329),
  scoped deploy 36285996570 attempt 1 and one bound own-ID REMOVED probe.
  Source/regression supports route-wide removal; no cross-user exploit test.
  Saved workflow/terminal evidence does not exclude out-of-band Azure changes.
  Advisor implementation removed in source by #332, not deployed.
  Header proof delivered by #331 within its recorded limits.
  No current HTTP advisor-to-Portfolio path; smoke/config/seed follow-ups stay open.
end note
note bottom of Gateway
  Internal seed/reset routes are public, no JWT/origin/route limiter.
  Downstream shared internal key gates those operations.
  Public market POST removed in #327; scoped deploy and Gate D confirmed removal.
  Historical-price integrity is not certified; optional audit skipped by owner.
  Manual demo-reset response carries an opaque replica token, not that key.
end note
note bottom of Frontend
  Logical source topology, not a live cloud inventory.
  Local Compose and retained AWS paths differ.
  Runtime verdict/evidence remain in the demo dashboard.
end note
@enduml
